lue "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id 17592186312423} {:answer/id #uuid "c9929a36-9c78-5386-8613-645d48af54de" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id 17592186313547} {:answer/id #uuid "f8854e4c-1476-5259-80df-34a5b76b1f6b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id 17592186313960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e41812a-03d8-5475-8f34-ec05ee42075a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id 17592186312338} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa2110c0-5101-54d7-887b-aa21835a6e99" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186314465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${b}_{2}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{2} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{b}_{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ & ={b}_{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ \\\\ {b}_{2} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩} \\\\ {b}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186314988 :question/id #uuid "b8b54f2c-8781-54b8-a107-16250836e9fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-340648"} {:db/id 17592186314989 :question/id #uuid "c36e0e36-a227-5df1-b273-538c9f56de6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-340652"} {:db/id 17592186314991 :question/id #uuid "dc60bc57-5b9c-5f88-9bc5-5ecffd1981e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-340662" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21c52c11-2a0f-58d6-aff5-fbcff80b806b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}" :db/id 17592186312230} {:answer/id #uuid "286e0c18-97d0-532c-bf41-6751830ae151" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩}" :db/id 17592186312282} {:answer/id #uuid "a350f6d6-24d8-5f63-b205-477f47e6d19e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}" :db/id 17592186313260} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b2f783-0c8d-5f89-9d7f-07e8c45faf2b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩}" :db/id 17592186313411} {:answer/id #uuid "e477c6c9-364e-5141-949d-9701044a0b0e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}" :db/id 17592186313778}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186312230} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cc086cc-8293-54fb-ab53-553c0b9185e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186314269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6adb5300-558b-5171-ae85-ccd08169caac" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186312814} {:answer/id #uuid "84bf4de8-2de1-5c8d-aa10-e8dc5e05701b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186313040} {:answer/id #uuid "b6112b1f-27d0-5ea9-9414-69665412c45e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186313389} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d80ee5-4b61-5649-991b-08f557a8dc02" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186313493} {:answer/id #uuid "ea34fcb0-83d8-5c60-9aab-be6de2adf3d8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186313839} {:answer/id #uuid "f1ab1a37-3aeb-50e5-ac0c-f636df7e8865" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186313911}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186312814} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3676550-2291-58a0-8716-0b0471438972" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186314451} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21099cf0-6ade-5176-97e2-98b51987b126" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id 17592186312226} {:answer/id #uuid "3f9b48c8-5e3a-5bc2-a5ab-b517fd3e8a59" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id 17592186312487} {:answer/id #uuid "5f73d4a2-4ad0-5837-b408-af5ab8f8dfdc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id 17592186312737} {:answer/id #uuid "b835c93d-0f3b-59f6-8a79-699819da02b4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id 17592186313406} {:answer/id #uuid "f35dc895-fc13-50f6-aa56-710cb0aafcfb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id 17592186313922}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186312737} :answer-field/id #uuid "f825e814-46db-5a49-9ae3-db2a2ad9a646" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186314683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487} :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}-6x$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${b}_{4}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{4} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{b}_{4}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{1}{16}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(16\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩ & ={b}_{4}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩ \\\\ {b}_{4} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)⟩} \\\\ {b}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{2}-6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186315082 :question/id #uuid "a5448f9e-c9df-59b5-abdc-33e558c56456" :question/math-academy-id "q-341309" :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "067f1f01-946a-508e-8cd3-212922a30cb6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id 17592186312018} {:answer/id #uuid "1c9ff7e5-36fe-5003-9799-45faaef030fe" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id 17592186312189} {:answer/id #uuid "7a6042f8-3d6d-5360-9b00-ffce5586d196" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id 17592186312954} {:answer/id #uuid "9d043cac-3ffa-5f03-90e2-e0c96f5392e5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id 17592186313218} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d8c3cb-4ca0-5236-8d59-7a3088019974" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id 17592186313774}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186313218} :answer-field/id #uuid "47c8bc7b-4cd5-5227-9be1-4358ff24b62e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186314211} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ffdb817-1342-5108-9142-29c41b65bfb6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186312744} {:answer/id #uuid "65761c3a-2090-56c5-acc5-a7f5ae659917" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186312774} {:answer/id #uuid "821891c1-b858-5bda-9626-34240d7900c4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186313023} {:answer/id #uuid "832cde4d-8aee-5316-8503-fd0c2df797ea" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186313031} {:answer/id #uuid "f1ae89cc-5e23-5a8d-aa64-bd8dbd7a3313" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186313912}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186313912} :answer-field/id #uuid "82f86a36-0a17-52e0-b0d0-d33c3e50f91e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186314358} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec31f7d-80af-523d-b38f-294b8ad028bb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨1,1⟩}{⟨f(x),1⟩}" :db/id 17592186312081} {:answer/id #uuid "0f14e142-4150-51d0-8ede-ebf4f1bd28f2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}" :db/id 17592186312085} {:answer/id #uuid "114b3cdc-ae09-538f-94d9-f5c3e4392e2b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩}" :db/id 17592186312098} {:answer/id #uuid "992303bc-e624-5324-b23d-d78df9b645e2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)⟩}" :db/id 17592186313189} {:answer/id #uuid "dd23267e-19c8-5ea7-b897-d3089e3d52ca" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩}" :db/id 17592186313714}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id 17592186312098} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0b3226d-31b8-5280-8683-73d653641be2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494} :db/id 17592186314547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485} :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{0}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),1⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),1⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),1⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨1,1⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),1⟩ & =\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩ \\\\ {a}_{0} & =\\frac{2⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩} \\\\ {a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186397418 :question/id #uuid "df849e8a-df1b-5b2f-bbc1-5b6e2ad9aeb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-340638" :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186166964 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "304c015d-cbb6-5989-a102-d6f0f5f38604" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Expressions For Fourier Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8748773f-b48a-58ec-b951-7e2f13629f66" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186397420} {:answer/id #uuid "0e3eeb27-01e0-5659-a89f-03c69d0adcb3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} 