answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "000cc7f2-c4e5-5aa6-9724-b55778b9ed16" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186547314} {:answer/id #uuid "296efdb0-b422-5a02-a76c-ccf2749a601d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186547393} {:answer/id #uuid "92d3bb01-ed2e-5352-80a8-a6aedbfc134e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186547641} {:answer/id #uuid "98857014-a914-550a-aa97-044d5b4c7812" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186547650} {:answer/id #uuid "df2d461c-bb5c-5c20-a3c7-9f0294a6bba6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186547780} {:answer/id #uuid "ee48b1a7-50cd-5e63-bcd3-da61e3a89995" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186547807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "000cc7f2-c4e5-5aa6-9724-b55778b9ed16" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id 17592186547314} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdf5d372-c050-5c3d-88c9-dcbaace4b624" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186547937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/problem "Let $F(x)=2{x}^{3}$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${b}_{2}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{2} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{b}_{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{1}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ & ={b}_{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩ \\\\ {b}_{2} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)⟩} \\\\ {b}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186050730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f77c573-2e4c-536e-af1e-09bf69080857" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186164763} {:answer/id #uuid "def9c8ed-19ee-58e5-969f-de9782068ef0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186164764} {:answer/id #uuid "37f67a97-5731-525d-8eea-9e2adde19ccb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id 17592186164765} {:answer/id #uuid "7a4cd2e6-0da4-5d24-b3e3-7bda7e4d5751" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186164766} {:answer/id #uuid "7ceba1a1-ec81-5071-86b8-40131cdb7eed" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186164767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f77c573-2e4c-536e-a